# Web API Development Patterns

## 🎯 **RESTful API Design**

### **Controller Structure:**
```csharp
[ApiController]
[Route("api/[controller]")]
[Authorize] // Global authorization
public class AccountController : BaseController
{
    private readonly IAccountService _accountService;
    private readonly IMapper _mapper;
    
    public AccountController(IAccountService accountService, IMapper mapper)
    {
        _accountService = accountService;
        _mapper = mapper;
    }
}
```

### **HTTP Method Conventions:**
```csharp
// GET - Retrieve resources
[HttpGet("{id}")]
public async Task<ActionResult<AccountDTO>> GetAccount(int id)

// POST - Create new resources
[HttpPost]
public async Task<ActionResult<AccountDTO>> CreateAccount([FromBody] CreateAccountDTO dto)

// PUT - Update entire resource
[HttpPut("{id}")]
public async Task<ActionResult<AccountDTO>> UpdateAccount(int id, [FromBody] UpdateAccountDTO dto)

// DELETE - Remove resources
[HttpDelete("{id}")]
public async Task<ActionResult> DeleteAccount(int id)
```

## 📝 **DTO Patterns**

### **Request/Response DTOs:**
```csharp
// Input DTOs (requests)
public class CreateAccountDTO
{
    [Required]
    [EmailAddress]
    public string Email { get; set; }
    
    [Required]
    [MinLength(6)]
    public string Password { get; set; }
    
    [Required]
    [MaxLength(250)]
    public string FirstName { get; set; }
    
    [Required]
    [MaxLength(250)]
    public string LastName { get; set; }
}

// Output DTOs (responses)
public class AccountDTO
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Email { get; set; }
    public string FirstName { get; set; }
    public string LastName { get; set; }
    public RoleEnum Role { get; set; }
    public DateTime Created { get; set; }
    public DateTime LastUpdated { get; set; }
}
```

### **DTO Naming Conventions:**
- **Create**: `Create{Entity}DTO` (e.g., `CreateAccountDTO`)
- **Update**: `Update{Entity}DTO` (e.g., `UpdateAccountDTO`)
- **Response**: `{Entity}DTO` (e.g., `AccountDTO`)
- **Specialized**: `{Purpose}{Entity}DTO` (e.g., `LoginAccountDTO`, `RefreshTokenDTO`)

## 🔄 **AutoMapper Configuration**

### **Mapping Profiles:**
```csharp
public class AccountProfile : Profile
{
    public AccountProfile()
    {
        // Entity to DTO
        CreateMap<Account, AccountDTO>()
            .ForMember(dest => dest.FullName, opt => opt.MapFrom(src => $"{src.FirstName} {src.LastName}"));
        
        // DTO to Entity
        CreateMap<CreateAccountDTO, Account>()
            .ForMember(dest => dest.Created, opt => opt.MapFrom(src => DateTime.UtcNow))
            .ForMember(dest => dest.LastUpdated, opt => opt.MapFrom(src => DateTime.UtcNow));
    }
}
```

### **Mapping Best Practices:**
- Use explicit mapping for complex transformations
- Ignore sensitive properties (passwords, tokens)
- Use `ForMember` for custom property mappings
- Create separate profiles for each entity

## 🔐 **Authentication & Authorization**

### **JWT Configuration:**
```json
{
  "Jwt": {
    "LifetimeMinutes": 30,
    "Key": "ihopethiskeyislongenough",
    "Issuer": "web-api-template",
    "Audience": "web-api-template-audience",
    "RefreshTokenExpiryDays": 7
  }
}
```

### **Authorization Patterns:**
```csharp
// Role-based authorization
[AuthorizeRoles(RoleEnum.Admin)]
public async Task<ActionResult> AdminOnlyAction()

// Custom authorization policies
[Authorize(Policy = nameof(IsUserLockedAuthHandler))]
public async Task<ActionResult> ProtectedAction()

// Allow anonymous for public endpoints
[AllowAnonymous]
[HttpPost("login")]
public async Task<ActionResult<LoginResponseDTO>> Login([FromBody] LoginAccountDTO dto)
```

## 📊 **Response Patterns**

### **Standard Response Format:**
```csharp
// Success responses
return Ok(accountDTO);
return CreatedAtAction(nameof(GetAccount), new { id = accountDTO.Id }, accountDTO);

// Error responses
return NotFound($"Account with ID {id} not found");
return BadRequest("Invalid input data");
return Unauthorized("Invalid credentials");
```

### **Exception Handling:**
```csharp
// Global exception handling in Program.cs
webApplication.HandleExceptions();

// Custom exception types
public class DomainException : Exception
{
    public DomainException(string message) : base(message) { }
}

// Service layer exception handling
public async Task<AccountDTO> CreateAccountAsync(CreateAccountDTO dto)
{
    try
    {
        var account = _mapper.Map<Account>(dto);
        await account.CreateAsync(_userManager, dto.Password);
        return _mapper.Map<AccountDTO>(account);
    }
    catch (DomainException ex)
    {
        throw; // Re-throw domain exceptions
    }
}
```

## 🚀 **Performance Optimization**

### **Async/Await Patterns:**
```csharp
// Always use async for I/O operations
public async Task<ActionResult<AccountDTO>> GetAccount(int id)
{
    var account = await _accountService.GetAccountAsync(id);
    if (account == null)
        return NotFound();
    
    return Ok(account);
}
```

### **Response Caching:**
```csharp
// Enable response caching in Program.cs
webApplication.UseResponseCaching();

// Cache specific endpoints
[ResponseCache(Duration = 300)] // 5 minutes
[HttpGet("{id}")]
public async Task<ActionResult<AccountDTO>> GetAccount(int id)
```

### **Compression:**
```csharp
// Enable response compression
webApplication.UseResponseCompression();
webApplication.UseCompressedStaticFiles(webApplication.Environment, webApplication.Services.GetRequiredService<IHttpContextAccessor>());
```

## 🧪 **API Testing**

### **Integration Test Patterns:**
```csharp
[Test]
public async Task CreateAccount_ValidInput_ReturnsCreatedAccount()
{
    // Arrange
    var createDto = new CreateAccountDTO
    {
        Email = "test@example.com",
        Password = "TestPassword123!",
        FirstName = "Test",
        LastName = "User"
    };
    
    // Act
    var response = await _client.PostAsJsonAsync("/api/account", createDto);
    
    // Assert
    response.StatusCode.Should().Be(HttpStatusCode.Created);
    var account = await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<AccountDTO>();
    account.Email.Should().Be(createDto.Email);
}
```

### **Test Base Configuration:**
```csharp
// Use BaseIntegrationTest for common setup
public class AccountTests : BaseIntegrationTest
{
    protected override void ConfigureServices(IServiceCollection services)
    {
        // Override services for testing
        services.AddScoped<IAccountService, MockAccountService>();
    }
}
```

## 📋 **API Documentation**

### **Swagger Configuration:**
```csharp
// Swagger setup in Program.cs
webApplication.UseSwagger(c =>
{
    c.RouteTemplate = "api/{documentname}/swagger.json";
});

webApplication.UseSwaggerUI(c =>
{
    c.SwaggerEndpoint("/api/v1/swagger.json", "asp-web-api template");
    c.RoutePrefix = "api";
});
```

### **API Documentation Best Practices:**
- Use XML comments for controller methods
- Provide example requests/responses
- Document error responses
- Use descriptive endpoint names
- Group related endpoints logically

## 🔧 **Health Checks**

### **Health Check Endpoints:**
```csharp
// Configure health checks in Program.cs
endpoints.MapHealthChecks("/health");

// Custom health checks
services.AddHealthChecks()
    .AddDbContext<ApplicationDbContext>()
    .AddCheck<DatabaseHealthCheck>("database");
```

### **Kubernetes Health Probes:**
```yaml
# Use /health endpoint for probes
livenessProbe:
  httpGet:
    path: /health
    port: 80
  initialDelaySeconds: 60
  periodSeconds: 15

readinessProbe:
  httpGet:
    path: /health
    port: 80
  initialDelaySeconds: 30
  periodSeconds: 10
```